    <briefdescription>
<para>The domain2D type contains all the necessary information to define the global, compute and data domains of each task, as well as the PE associated with the task. The PEs from which remote data may be acquired to update the data domain are also contained in a linked list of neighbours. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Domain types of higher rank can be constructed from type domain1D typically we only need 1 and 2D, but could need higher (e.g 3D LES) some elements are repeated below if they are needed once per domain, not once per axis </para>    </detaileddescription>
